Problem: Which cities, stations, or sites spend the highest number of days/hours in Poor, Very Poor, or Severe AQI buckets?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Solution:
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
I created Hours_Poor_to_Severe KPIs for cities and monitoring stations to count the recorded hours when the AQI was classified as Poor, Very Poor, or Severe.
I then used the Top_3_Poor_to_Severe measures to identify and display the three cities and stations with the highest number of these unhealthy hours.

DAX :  
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Hours_Poor_to_Severe_City = 

 CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS('goldlayer fact_cities'),
    'goldlayer fact_cities'[AQI Bucket] IN {"Poor","Very Poor","Severe"}
)

Top_3_Poor_to_Severe_cities = 
    VAR AQI_rank = IF(
        NOT ISBLANK([Hours_Poor_to_Severe_City]),
        CALCULATE(
            RANKX(ALLSELECTED('goldlayer fact_cities'[city]),
            [Hours_Poor_to_Severe_City],,DESC,Dense)
        )
    )
    
RETURN
IF(
    AQI_rank <= 3, [Hours_Poor_to_Severe_City],BLANK())


Hours_Poor_to_Severe_Station = 
CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS('goldlayer fact_stations'),
    'goldlayer fact_cities'[AQI Bucket] IN {"Poor","Very Poor","Severe"}
)


Top_3_Stations_Poor_to_Severe_hour = 
VAR Aqi_station_rank = 
IF(
  NOT ISBLANK([Hours_Poor_to_Severe_Station]),
CALCULATE(
    RANKX(
        ALLSELECTED('goldlayer fact_stations'),
        [Hours_Poor_to_Severe_Station],,
        DESC,Dense
    )
),BLANK())

RETURN
IF(
Aqi_station_rank <=3, [Hours_Poor_to_Severe_Station],BLANK())


Problem : How frequently do individual pollutants breach safe thresholds?

Solution:

To determine how frequently pollutant levels exceeded safe limits, I calculated the hourly count of instances in which each pollutant surpassed its defined moderate threshold.
I then added the pollutant field as a slicer, enabling users to analyze exceedance frequency by city and monitoring station.
Finally, I created a dynamic measure that displays the threshold-breach frequency for the selected pollutant.

PM2.5_Severe breach frequency_City = 
CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS('goldlayer fact_cities'),
    'goldlayer fact_cities'[pm2.5] > 90)
======================================================================
PM10_Severe breach frequency_City = 
CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS('goldlayer fact_cities'),
    'goldlayer fact_cities'[pm10] > 250)
======================================================================
NO2_Severe breach frequency_Cities = 
CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS('goldlayer fact_cities'),
'goldlayer fact_cities'[no2] > 180)
======================================================================

SO2_Severe breach frequency_Cities = 
CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS('goldlayer fact_cities'),
'goldlayer fact_cities'[so2] > 380)
======================================================================
NH3_Severe breach frequency_Cities = 
CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS('goldlayer fact_cities'),
'goldlayer fact_cities'[nh3] > 800)
======================================================================

CO_Sever breach frequency_City = 
CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS('goldlayer fact_cities'),
'goldlayer fact_cities'[co] > 10)
======================================================================

O3_Severe breach frequency_Cities = 
CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS('goldlayer fact_cities'),
'goldlayer fact_cities'[o3] > 168)
===========================================================================

****Did the same calculation for monitoring  Stations******

Value_City = 
SWITCH(
    [Selected Pollutant],
